\end_layout

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
I find the optimal deterministic classification rule by applying Bayes-optimal rule under 0-1 loss.
 This means choosing the value of 
\begin_inset Formula $\hat{y}$
\end_inset

 which maximizes the probability of 
\begin_inset Formula $\hat{y}=y$
\end_inset

 given the input variable 
\begin_inset Formula $x$
\end_inset

:
 
\begin_inset Formula 
\[
\hat{y}\left(x\right)=\arg\max_{y\in\{0,1\}}P\left(Y=y\mid X=x\right).
\]

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Applying this yields:
 
\begin_inset Formula 
\[
\hat{y}=0\quad\text{for all }x\in\left\{ 0,1\right\} .
\]

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Assuming that 
\begin_inset Formula $P\left(X=0\right)=P\left(X=1\right)=0.5$
\end_inset

,
 i get the expected 0-1 loss:
 
\begin_inset Formula 
\begin{align*}
\mathcal{R}_{p}\left(\hat{y}\left(X\right)\right) & =\mathbb{E}_{X}\left[P\left(Y\neq\hat{y}\left(X)\right)\mid X\right)\right],\\
 & =P\left(X=0\right)P\left(Y\neq\hat{y}\left(0)\right)\right)+P\left(X=1\right)P\left(Y\neq\hat{y}\left(1)\right)\right),\\
 & =0.5\cdot P\left(Y=1\mid X=0\right)+0.5\cdot P\left(Y=1\mid X=1\right),\\
 & =0.5\cdot0+0.5\cdot0.2,\\
 & =0.1.
\end{align*}

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsection*
Question 2
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset ERT
status collapsed

\begin_layout Plain Layout

\backslash
addcontentsline{toc}{subsection}{Question 2}
\end_layout

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
With the new probabilistic classifier:
 
\begin_inset Formula 
\[
\hat{y}=\begin{cases}
0 & \text{for }x=0\\
P\left(\hat{y}=0\right)=0.8\text{ and }P\left(\hat{y}=1\right)=0.2 & \text{for }x=1
\end{cases},
\]

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
the expected 0-1 loss is:
 
\begin_inset Formula 
\begin{align*}
\mathcal{R}_{p}\left(\hat{y}\left(X\right)\right) & =P\left(X=0\right)P\left(\hat{y}\neq Y\mid X=0\right)+P\left(X=1\right)P\left(\hat{y}\neq Y\mid X=1\right),\\
 & =0.5P\left(Y=1\mid X=0\right)+\\
 & \quad0.5\left(P\left(\hat{y}=0\mid X=1\right)P\left(Y=1\mid X=1\right)+P\left(\hat{y}=1\mid X=1\right)P\left(Y=0\mid X=1\right)\right),\\
 & =0.5\cdot0+0.5\left(0.8\cdot0.2+0.2\cdot0.8\right),\\
 & =0.16.
\end{align*}

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsection*
Question 3
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset ERT
