\begin_layout Subsubsection
Logistic regression
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
I used python to apply the multinomial logistic regression (numpy and scikit-learn).
 I used stochastic gradient descent (SGD) to fit the model,
 with a tolerance of 
\begin_inset Formula $1\cdot10^{-8}$
\end_inset

.
 I did not use any regularization as using two-norm regularization didn't improve the 0-1 loss meaningfully for any values of 
\begin_inset Formula $C$
\end_inset

.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Using logistic regression with no regularization,
 i got a training 0-1 loss of 
\begin_inset Formula $L_{train}(h)=\frac{1}{n}\sum^{n}_{i=1}\boldsymbol{1}[h(\boldsymbol{x}_{train,i})\neq y_{train,i}]\approx0.1495,$
\end_inset

and a test 0-1 loss of 
\begin_inset Formula $L_{test}(h)\approx0.0956$
\end_inset

.
\end_layout

